# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD rod-A 32054 black
ADD axle-A 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-A.axle1 -> rod-A.axlehole1 LOCKED
DOES rod-A HOLDS axle-A
PATTERN pin_axle_pin_shaft
WHY Starts a straight cross shaft for the middle of the undercarriage; A long pin with a stop ring has a pin on one end (to hang beams on) and an axle hole on the other (to join an axle).

STEP 2
ADD beam-C 63869 lightgray
ADD rod-B 32054 black
CONNECT axle-A.axle2 -> beam-C.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-A.axle3 -> rod-B.axlehole1 LOCKED
DOES axle-A CARRIES beam-C
DOES rod-B HOLDS axle-A
DOES rod-A LOCKS beam-C
DOES rod-B LOCKS beam-C
PATTERN trapped_connector
WHY Finishes the cross shaft and gives it a mounting point in the middle; The triple connector turns one axle into three pin holes facing sideways; the two rings trap it so it can't slide.

STEP 3
ADD bentbeam-D 32140 black
ADD pin-E 2780 black
ADD pin-F 2780 black
CONNECT rod-B.pin2 -> bentbeam-D.hole4 STIFF
CONNECT pin-E.pin1 -> beam-C.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT pin-F.pin1 -> beam-C.hole3 STIFF
DOES rod-B HOLDS bentbeam-D
DOES beam-C HOLDS pin-E
DOES beam-C HOLDS pin-F
PATTERN two_pin_mount
WHY Starts one side of the front frame and readies the turntable mount; An L-shaped beam goes up and over the shaft, then runs forward; two pins give a firm two-point grip.

STEP 4
ADD axle-red-G 32062 red
ADD connector-H 6536 black
CONNECT axle-red-G.axle1 -> bentbeam-D.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT connector-H.axlehole1 -> axle-red-G.axle2 LOCKED
DOES bentbeam-D HOLDS axle-red-G
DOES axle-red-G CARRIES connector-H
PATTERN change_direction
WHY Gives the front corner a pin hole facing up; The connector has an axle hole and a pin hole at right angles, so it turns a sideways axle into an upward hole.

STEP 5
ADD bentbeam-I 32140 black
ADD axle-red-J 32062 red
ADD connector-K 6536 black
CONNECT axle-red-J.axle1 -> connector-K.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-red-J.axle2 -> bentbeam-I.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT rod-A.pin2 -> bentbeam-I.hole4 STIFF
DOES connector-K HOLDS axle-red-J
DOES bentbeam-I HOLDS axle-red-J
DOES rod-A HOLDS bentbeam-I
PATTERN mirror_side
WHY Builds the other side so the frame is the same on both sides; Same parts as steps 3-4, so the two sides match.

STEP 6
ADD pin-L 2780 black
ADD pin-M 2780 black
CONNECT pin-L.pin1 -> connector-H.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT pin-M.pin1 -> connector-K.hole1 STIFF
DOES connector-H HOLDS pin-L
DOES connector-K HOLDS pin-M
PATTERN pegs_for_crossbar
WHY Gives the front corners pegs to hang a crossbar on; Plain friction pins hold firmly without spinning loose.

STEP 7
ADD beam7-N 32524 black
CONNECT pin-L.pin2 -> beam7-N.hole3 STIFF
CONNECT pin-M.pin2 -> beam7-N.hole5 STIFF
DOES pin-L LOCKS beam7-N
DOES pin-M LOCKS beam7-N
DOES beam7-N SUPPORTS bentbeam-D
DOES beam7-N SUPPORTS bentbeam-I
PATTERN closed_box_frame
WHY Closes the U so the two sides can't spread or twist; A 7-hole beam is long enough to span both front corners.

STEP 8
ADD turntable-O 50163 darkgray
CONNECT pin-E.pin2 -> turntable-O.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-F.pin2 -> turntable-O.hole11~ STIFF
DOES pin-E HOLDS turntable-O
DOES pin-F HOLDS turntable-O
DOES turntable-O.top SPINS_ON turntable-O.base
PATTERN turntable_joint
DOES turntable-O SUPPORTS seat
WHY Adds the joint that lets the whole upper body turn all the way around; This big turntable has two halves that turn against each other, with 24 teeth inside and 56 outside for a gear to drive later.

STEP 9
ADD pin-P 2780 black
ADD pin-Q 2780 black
ADD beam-R 63869 lightgray
CONNECT pin-P.pin1 -> turntable-O.hole4~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-Q.pin1 -> turntable-O.hole13~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-P.pin2 -> beam-R.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT pin-Q.pin2 -> beam-R.hole3 STIFF
DOES turntable-O HOLDS pin-P
DOES turntable-O HOLDS pin-Q
DOES pin-P LOCKS beam-R
DOES pin-Q LOCKS beam-R
PATTERN two_pin_mount
WHY Adds a back mounting point so the turntable is held at both front and back; The same triple connector as beam-C, now at the back, gives a matching axle hole for a back cross bar.

STEP 10
ADD axle-S 4519 lightgray
ADD connector-T 59443 black
ADD pin-U 43093 blue
CONNECT axle-S.axle3 -> connector-T.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-U.axle1 -> connector-T.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-S.axle2 -> beam-R.axlehole1 LOCKED
DOES beam-R HOLDS axle-S
DOES axle-S CARRIES connector-T
DOES connector-T HOLDS pin-U
PATTERN axle_to_pin_end
WHY Starts a back cross bar reaching out to the right side rail; The axle connector extends the axle, and the blue axle pin turns its end into a pin for a beam to hang on.

STEP 11
ADD connector-W 59443 black
ADD pin-V 43093 blue
CONNECT axle-S.axle1 -> connector-W.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-V.axle1 -> connector-W.axlehole2 LOCKED
DOES axle-S CARRIES connector-W
DOES connector-W HOLDS pin-V
PATTERN mirror_side
WHY Finishes the back cross bar on the left side; Same parts as step 10, so both sides match.

STEP 12
ADD beam9-X 40490 black
ADD beam9-Y 40490 black
CONNECT rod-B.pin2 -> beam9-X.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT pin-V.pin1 -> beam9-X.hole8 STIFF
CONNECT rod-A.pin2 -> beam9-Y.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT pin-U.pin1 -> beam9-Y.hole8 STIFF
DOES rod-B HOLDS beam9-X
DOES pin-V HOLDS beam9-X
DOES rod-A HOLDS beam9-Y
DOES pin-U HOLDS beam9-Y
PATTERN side_rails
DOES beam9-X SUPPORTS track-left
DOES beam9-Y SUPPORTS track-right
WHY Ties front and back into one stiff base and sets the track length; 9-hole beams reach from the shaft to the back cross bar with a hole left over at each end.

STEP 13
ADD tan-1 3749 tan
ADD tan-2 3749 tan
ADD tan-3 3749 tan
ADD tan-4 3749 tan
CONNECT tan-1.pin1 -> beam9-X.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT tan-2.pin1 -> beam9-X.hole9 TURNS
CONNECT tan-3.pin1 -> beam9-Y.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT tan-4.pin1 -> beam9-Y.hole9 TURNS
DOES tan-1 SPINS_ON beam9-X
DOES tan-2 SPINS_ON beam9-X
DOES tan-3 SPINS_ON beam9-Y
DOES tan-4 SPINS_ON beam9-Y
PATTERN free_spinning_axle
WHY Adds four wheel axles that turn freely; Tan pins have no friction ridges, so they spin easily; their axle ends will grip a gear.

STEP 14
ADD gear-1 4019 lightgray
ADD gear-2 4019 lightgray
ADD gear-3 4019 lightgray
ADD gear-4 4019 lightgray
CONNECT gear-1.axlehole1 -> tan-1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-2.axlehole1 -> tan-2.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-3.axlehole1 -> tan-3.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-4.axlehole1 -> tan-4.axle1 LOCKED
MESH tread-?.teeth gear-1.teeth
MESH tread-?.teeth gear-2.teeth
MESH tread-?.teeth gear-3.teeth
MESH tread-?.teeth gear-4.teeth
DOES tan-1 CARRIES gear-1
DOES tan-2 CARRIES gear-2
DOES tan-3 CARRIES gear-3
DOES tan-4 CARRIES gear-4
PATTERN gears_as_track_wheels
DOES gear-1 HOLDS track-left
DOES gear-2 HOLDS track-left
DOES gear-3 HOLDS track-right
DOES gear-4 HOLDS track-right
WHY Adds the wheels the tracks run around; The tread links have teeth that mesh with a 16-tooth gear, so a gear works as a track wheel.

STEP 15
ADD tread-1 3873 black
ADD tread-2 3873 black
ADD tread-3 3873 black
ADD tread-4 3873 black
ADD tread-5 3873 black
ADD tread-6 3873 black
ADD tread-7 3873 black
ADD tread-8 3873 black
ADD tread-9 3873 black
ADD tread-10 3873 black
ADD tread-11 3873 black
ADD tread-12 3873 black
ADD tread-13 3873 black
ADD tread-14 3873 black
ADD tread-15 3873 black
ADD tread-16 3873 black
ADD tread-17 3873 black
ADD tread-18 3873 black
ADD tread-19 3873 black
ADD tread-20 3873 black
ADD tread-21 3873 black
ADD tread-22 3873 black
ADD tread-23 3873 black
ADD tread-24 3873 black
ADD tread-25 3873 black
ADD tread-26 3873 black
ADD tread-27 3873 black
ADD tread-28 3873 black
ADD tread-29 3873 black
ADD tread-30 3873 black
ADD tread-31 3873 black
ADD tread-32 3873 black
ADD tread-33 3873 black
ADD tread-34 3873 black
ADD tread-35 3873 black
ADD tread-36 3873 black
ADD tread-37 3873 black
ADD tread-38 3873 black
ADD tread-39 3873 black
ADD tread-40 3873 black
ADD tread-41 3873 black
ADD tread-42 3873 black
ADD tread-43 3873 black
ADD tread-44 3873 black
ADD tread-45 3873 black
ADD tread-46 3873 black
ADD tread-47 3873 black
ADD tread-48 3873 black
ADD tread-49 3873 black
ADD tread-50 3873 black
ADD tread-51 3873 black
ADD tread-52 3873 black
ADD tread-53 3873 black
ADD tread-54 3873 black
ADD tread-55 3873 black
ADD tread-56 3873 black
CONNECT tread-1.bar2 -> tread-2.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-2.bar2 -> tread-3.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-3.bar2 -> tread-4.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-4.bar2 -> tread-5.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-5.bar2 -> tread-6.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-6.bar2 -> tread-7.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-7.bar2 -> tread-8.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-8.bar2 -> tread-9.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-9.bar2 -> tread-10.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-10.bar2 -> tread-11.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-11.bar2 -> tread-12.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-12.bar2 -> tread-13.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-13.bar2 -> tread-14.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-14.bar2 -> tread-15.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-15.bar2 -> tread-16.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-16.bar2 -> tread-17.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-17.bar2 -> tread-18.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-18.bar2 -> tread-19.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-19.bar2 -> tread-20.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-20.bar2 -> tread-21.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-21.bar2 -> tread-22.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-22.bar2 -> tread-23.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-23.bar2 -> tread-24.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-24.bar2 -> tread-25.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-25.bar2 -> tread-26.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-26.bar2 -> tread-27.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-27.bar2 -> tread-28.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-28.bar2 -> tread-1.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-29.bar2 -> tread-30.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-30.bar2 -> tread-31.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-31.bar2 -> tread-32.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-32.bar2 -> tread-33.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-33.bar2 -> tread-34.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-34.bar2 -> tread-35.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-35.bar2 -> tread-36.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-36.bar2 -> tread-37.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-37.bar2 -> tread-38.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-38.bar2 -> tread-39.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-39.bar2 -> tread-40.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-40.bar2 -> tread-41.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-41.bar2 -> tread-42.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-42.bar2 -> tread-43.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-43.bar2 -> tread-44.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-44.bar2 -> tread-45.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-45.bar2 -> tread-46.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-46.bar2 -> tread-47.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-47.bar2 -> tread-48.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-48.bar2 -> tread-49.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-49.bar2 -> tread-50.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-50.bar2 -> tread-51.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-51.bar2 -> tread-52.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-52.bar2 -> tread-53.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-53.bar2 -> tread-54.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-54.bar2 -> tread-55.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-55.bar2 -> tread-56.clip1 TURNS
CONNECT tread-56.bar2 -> tread-29.clip1 TURNS
PATTERN track_loop_on_idlers
WHY Gives the excavator its tracks; Tread links clip into a loop of any length and their teeth fit a 16-tooth gear, so two gears per side make a track.

STEP 16
ADD pinlong-1 6558 blue
ADD pinlong-2 6558 blue
CONNECT pinlong-1.pin1 -> turntable-O.hole5~ STIFF
CONNECT pinlong-2.pin1 -> turntable-O.hole8~ STIFF
DOES turntable-O HOLDS pinlong-1
DOES turntable-O HOLDS pinlong-2
PATTERN pins_as_mounting_posts
DOES pinlong-1 HOLDS seat
DOES pinlong-2 HOLDS seat
DOES pinlong-1 LOCKS seat
DOES pinlong-2 LOCKS seat
WHY Gives the turning half of the turntable two mounting pins; Long pins stick out far enough to take a beam on their free half.

STEP 17
GROUP seat
ADD hub4-s 48989 lightgray
ADD pin-s1 6558 blue
ADD hub2-s 87082 lightgray
CONNECT pin-s1.pin2 -> hub4-s.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT hub2-s.pin1 -> hub4-s.hole1 STIFF
DOES hub4-s HOLDS pin-s1
DOES hub4-s HOLDS hub2-s
WHY Starts the seat frame with a block that has pins pointing in many directions; Hub connectors turn one spot into pins facing three ways, so beams can be added at right angles.

STEP 18
ADD lbeam-s1 32526 blue
CONNECT lbeam-s1.hole5~ -> hub4-s.pin1~ STIFF
DOES hub4-s HOLDS lbeam-s1
WHY Adds the seat back; An L-beam gives a seat and a back in one part.

STEP 19
ADD beam5-s 32316 lightgray
ADD pin-s2 6558 blue
ADD pin-s3 6558 blue
CONNECT pin-s2.pin2 -> beam5-s.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT pin-s2.pin1 -> lbeam-s1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT pin-s3.pin2 -> beam5-s.hole4 STIFF
CONNECT pin-s3.pin1 -> lbeam-s1.hole4 STIFF
DOES beam5-s HOLDS pin-s2
DOES beam5-s HOLDS pin-s3
DOES pin-s2 LOCKS beam5-s
DOES pin-s3 LOCKS beam5-s
WHY Thickens the seat back and gives it two forward pins; A straight 5-beam lines up with the L-beam's long arm.

STEP 20
ADD lbeam-s2 32526 blue
CONNECT pin-s2.pin3 -> lbeam-s2.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT pin-s3.pin3 -> lbeam-s2.hole4 STIFF
DOES pin-s2 LOCKS lbeam-s2
DOES pin-s3 LOCKS lbeam-s2
WHY Closes the seat into a solid block; Same L-beam as step 2, mirrored around the gray beam.

STEP 21
ADD conn-s1 42003 black
ADD block-s 60483 lightgray
CONNECT block-s.hole1 -> hub4-s.pin4~ STIFF
CONNECT conn-s1.hole1~ -> hub4-s.pin3~ STIFF
DOES hub4-s HOLDS block-s
DOES hub4-s HOLDS conn-s1
WHY Adds axle holes under the seat; These connectors change pins into axle holes.

STEP 22
ADD axle9-s1 60485 lightgray
CONNECT axle9-s1.axle5 -> conn-s1.axlehole1 LOCKED
DOES conn-s1 HOLDS axle9-s1
WHY Adds the first cross bar of the seat frame; A long axle reaches both side beams of the frame.

STEP 23
ADD gear-5 4019 lightgray
ADD axle7-s 44294 lightgray
ADD bush-s1 3713 lightgray
CONNECT gear-5.axlehole1 -> axle7-s.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle7-s.axle4~ -> hub4-s.hole3~ TURNS
CONNECT bush-s1.axlehole1 -> axle7-s.axle7 LOCKED
DOES axle7-s CARRIES gear-5
DOES bush-s1 LOCKS axle7-s
WHY Adds a turning shaft with a gear; A bush keeps an axle from sliding out without stopping it from turning.

STEP 24
ADD lbeam-s3 32526 darkgray
CONNECT axle9-s1.axle1 -> lbeam-s3.hole5~ TURNS
DOES axle9-s1 CARRIES lbeam-s3
WHY Adds the left side of the seat frame; An L-beam gives a side and a leg in one part.

STEP 25
ADD bush-s2 3713 lightgray
CONNECT bush-s2.axlehole1 -> axle9-s1.axle1 LOCKED
DOES bush-s2 LOCKS lbeam-s3
WHY Stops lbeam-s3 sliding off; A bush grips the axle end.

STEP 26
ADD axle9-s2 60485 lightgray
ADD bush-s3 3713 lightgray
CONNECT bush-s3.axlehole1 -> axle9-s2.axle5 LOCKED
CONNECT axle9-s2.axle5~ -> block-s.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle9-s2.axle1 -> lbeam-s3.hole3~ TURNS
DOES lbeam-s3 HOLDS axle9-s2
DOES bush-s3 LOCKS axle9-s2
WHY Adds the second cross bar of the seat frame; Two axles keep the side beams from twisting.

STEP 27
ADD lbeam-s4 32526 darkgray
ADD crown-1 3650c lightgray
CONNECT axle9-s1.axle9 -> lbeam-s4.hole5~ TURNS
CONNECT axle9-s2.axle9 -> lbeam-s4.hole3~ TURNS
CONNECT crown-1.axlehole1 -> axle7-s.axle7 LOCKED
END
DOES axle9-s1 CARRIES lbeam-s4
DOES axle9-s2 CARRIES lbeam-s4
DOES axle7-s CARRIES crown-1
WHY Closes the seat frame and finishes the gear shaft; A crown gear can mesh with a gear at right angles.

STEP 28
ATTACH seat
CONNECT pinlong-1.pin3 -> lbeam-s3.hole7~ STIFF
CONNECT pinlong-2.pin3 -> lbeam-s4.hole7~ STIFF
PATTERN pin_hub_core
PATTERN l_beam_as_seat
PATTERN doubled_upright
PATTERN mirror_side
PATTERN pin_to_axlehole_adapter
PATTERN axle_as_cross_bar
PATTERN shaft_with_gear_and_bush
PATTERN l_beam_side_plate
PATTERN bush_as_end_stop
PATTERN two_bar_frame
PATTERN mirror_side
PATTERN upper_body_on_turntable
WHY Puts the seat on the turning half; Mounting on the turntable lets the whole upper body turn on the tracks.

STEP 29
CONNECT pinlong-1.pin3 -> lbeam-s3.hole7~ STIFF
CONNECT pinlong-2.pin3 -> lbeam-s4.hole7~ STIFF
PATTERN push_pins_home
WHY Locks the seat build down so it can't lift off; No new parts: pushing the long pins home is enough.

STEP 30
ADD axle7-B 44294 lightgray
ADD axcon-1 59443 black
ADD axpin-1 43093 blue
ADD conn3-1 42003 black
CONNECT axle7-B.axle1 -> axcon-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axpin-1.axle1 -> axcon-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT axle7-B.axle2~ -> lbeam-s3.hole6~ TURNS
CONNECT axle7-B.axle6~ -> lbeam-s4.hole6~ TURNS
CONNECT conn3-1.axlehole1 -> axle9-s2.axle1 LOCKED
DOES axcon-1 HOLDS axpin-1
DOES axle9-s2 CARRIES conn3-1
DOES lbeam-s3 HOLDS axle7-B
PATTERN axle_to_pin_shaft
WHY Adds a long cross shaft under the seat for the side frames to hang on; An axle connector plus axle pin turns an axle end into a pin, so a beam can swing on it.

STEP 31
ADD bent11-A 32009 black
CONNECT axpin-1.pin1 -> bent11-A.hole1 STIFF
DOES axpin-1 HOLDS bent11-A
PATTERN bent_beam_side_frame
DOES bent11-A SUPPORTS body
WHY Starts the side frame of the upper body; A double-bent beam goes round the turntable and rises at the back in one part.

STEP 32
ADD pin-21a 2780 black
ADD pin-21b 2780 black
ADD axle3-21 4519 lightgray
CONNECT pin-21a.pin1 -> bent11-A.hole8~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-21b.pin1 -> bent11-A.hole7~ STIFF
CONNECT axle3-21.axle1 -> bent11-A.hole3~ TURNS
DOES bent11-A HOLDS pin-21a
DOES bent11-A HOLDS pin-21b
DOES bent11-A HOLDS axle3-21
PATTERN pins_as_mounting_posts
WHY Adds mounting points on the side frame; Friction pins and a short axle let the yellow body clip on later.

STEP 33
ADD conn3c-1 32184 lightgray
ADD gear-6 4019 lightgray
CONNECT conn3c-1.axlehole1 -> axle9-s1.axle9 LOCKED
CONNECT conn3c-1.axlehole2 -> axle9-s2.axle9 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-6.axlehole1 -> axle7-B.axle7 LOCKED
MESH gear-5.teeth gear-6.teeth
RATIO gear-5 gear-6 16/16
DOES axle7-B CARRIES gear-6
DOES gear-5 DRIVES gear-6
DOES conn3c-1 HOLDS axle9-s1
PATTERN gear_pair_1to1
WHY Links the seat gear shaft to the long shaft; Two 16-tooth gears pass turning on at 1:1.

STEP 34
ADD link9-1 64451 darkgray
ADD crank-1 33299a lightgray
CONNECT crank-1.pin1 -> link9-1.hole1 STIFF
DOES crank-1 HOLDS link9-1
DOES link9-1 SPINS_ON crank-1
PATTERN crank_and_link_lever
DOES link9-1 HOLDS arm
WHY Adds a lever in front of the seat; A crank plus a bent link makes a lever that swings.

STEP 35
ADD bent11-B 32009 black
CONNECT pinlong-1.pin3 -> bent11-B.hole1 STIFF
DOES pinlong-1 HOLDS bent11-B
PATTERN mirror_side
DOES bent11-B SUPPORTS body
WHY Adds the second side frame; Same part as step 20, mirrored.

STEP 36
ADD pin-25a 2780 black
ADD pin-25b 2780 black
ADD axle3-25 4519 lightgray
CONNECT pin-25a.pin1 -> bent11-B.hole8~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-25b.pin1 -> bent11-B.hole7~ STIFF
CONNECT axle3-25.axle1 -> bent11-B.hole3~ TURNS
DOES bent11-B HOLDS pin-25a
DOES bent11-B HOLDS pin-25b
DOES bent11-B HOLDS axle3-25
PATTERN mirror_side
WHY Matches step 21 on this side; Same parts, mirrored.

STEP 37
ADD axle8s-1 55013 darkgray
ADD conn3-2 42003 black
ADD worm-1 4716 lightgray
ADD bush-26 3713 lightgray
CONNECT axle8s-1.axle4~ -> conn3-2.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT worm-1.axlehole1 -> axle8s-1.axle4 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-26.axlehole1 -> axle8s-1.axle8 LOCKED
MESH worm-1.teeth crown-1.teeth
RATIO worm-1 crown-1 1/24
DOES axle8s-1 CARRIES worm-1
DOES worm-1 DRIVES crown-1
DOES bush-26 LOCKS axle8s-1
DOES axle8s-1 SPINS_ON conn3-2
PATTERN worm_drive
WHY Adds the slow drive for the gear train; A worm only turns the gear, never the other way, so the upper body stays where you leave it.

STEP 38
ADD bush-27 3713 lightgray
CONNECT bush-27.axlehole1 -> axle3-21.axle3 LOCKED
DOES bush-27 LOCKS axle3-21
PATTERN bush_as_end_stop
WHY Stops an axle sliding out; A bush grips the axle end.

STEP 39
ADD bush-28 3713 lightgray
CONNECT bush-28.axlehole1 -> axle7-s.axle7 LOCKED
DOES bush-28 LOCKS axle7-s
PATTERN bush_as_end_stop
WHY Keeps the crown gear shaft from sliding; A bush lets the shaft spin but not slide.

STEP 40
WHY Shows the back so the yellow body can go on; View change only.

STEP 41
GROUP body
ADD pin-b1 6558 blue
